  "map_version": "vertical_map_v1",
  "written": "2026-10-07",
  "rule": "A vertical name is matched by exact key or alias after normalisation (lower case, spaces and hyphens to underscores, then a singular/plural retry). No fuzzy or substring matching: 'lawn care' must never match 'law'. The matched KEY is what the engine policy sees, so a key here can sit on an engine's relevant_verticals list.",
  "basis": "Every audience and local value below is an operator classification [EST]: who asks an assistant about this vertical, a member of the public (b2c), a business buyer (b2b), or both (mixed). No usage data sits behind any row.",
  "amendment_rule": "Rows may be ADDED in place. Changing an existing row's audience or local value is vertical_map_v2.json with the reason stated, because it changes which engines a past profile would have picked.",
  "unclassified": {
    "audience": "mixed",
    "local": false,
    "basis": "A vertical not on the map is treated as mixed, so no engine is dropped on a guess. The plan prints VERTICAL_UNCLASSIFIED. Cost of this choice: an unlisted consumer vertical calls Claude and Perplexity until a row is added or --audience is passed."
  },
